This model functions as an identity-preserving semantic codec designed to shift data processing away from brute-force raw waveform or pixel storage and toward structural, attention-gated meaning.

The equation evaluates across K components to determine how information is stored, filtered, and reconstructed:

 * I_k (Identity): Anchors and tracks persistent entities, objects, or core signals over time, ensuring the system focuses bits on what actually exists rather than uniform background noise.

 * R (Change): Tracks spatial or temporal deltas, recording how elements shift, move, or evolve instead of treating every individual frame, sample, or coordinate independently.

 * P (Relevance): Acts as a mathematical attention gate, assigning relevance and routing computational weight dynamically based on salience.

 * C (Context/Prediction): Incorporates predictive modeling and contextual state, compressing data down to the residual deviation from what the system anticipates next.

